cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use PyRPMD, please cite the software as below and record the exact
  version or commit. Also cite the original method, potential-energy-surface
  and upstream-software papers for the features you used; they are listed in
  docs/manual/references.md and docs/references.bib.
type: software
title: "PyRPMD: ring-polymer dynamics, reaction networks and adaptive free-energy sampling"
abstract: >-
  PyRPMD runs ring-polymer molecular dynamics from a single Python or TOML
  input: bimolecular RPMD rates from a transition state, direct collisions,
  free-energy surfaces and enhanced sampling, path-integral molecular dynamics,
  periodic materials and surfaces, nonadiabatic ring-polymer methods and
  electrochemical proton-coupled electron transfer, with restartable
  checkpoints and C++/OpenMP kernels alongside a NumPy reference.
authors:
  - name: PyRPMD contributors
version: 0.2.0
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/chen-yu-hao/PyRPMD"
url: "https://github.com/chen-yu-hao/PyRPMD/blob/main/docs/index.md"
keywords:
  - ring-polymer molecular dynamics
  - path-integral molecular dynamics
  - nuclear quantum effects
  - reaction rates
  - free-energy calculations
  - enhanced sampling
  - nonadiabatic dynamics
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Suleimanov
        given-names: Y. V.
      - family-names: Allen
        given-names: J. W.
      - family-names: Green
        given-names: W. H.
    title: "RPMDrate: Bimolecular chemical reaction rates from ring polymer molecular dynamics"
    journal: Computer Physics Communications
    volume: 184
    start: 833
    end: 840
    year: 2013
    doi: 10.1016/j.cpc.2012.10.017
    notes: Source of the adapted Cayley integrator, reaction coordinate and rate algorithms.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Steffen
        given-names: J.
    title: "Caracal: A Versatile Ring Polymer Molecular Dynamics Simulation Package"
    journal: Journal of Chemical Theory and Computation
    volume: 19
    start: 5334
    end: 5355
    year: 2023
    doi: 10.1021/acs.jctc.3c00568
    notes: Umbrella-sampling and recrossing workflow organization followed by the rate workflow.
